# Local stow ignore for the `hypr` package.
# Presence of this file overrides .stow-global-ignore for this package only,
# allowing the hypr config files committed under this package to be stowed
# while the global ignore continues to protect every other package from
# leaking hypr configs.
#
# Defensive: keep TRULY machine-specific hardware configs out even if they
# ever end up under hypr/.config/hypr/ by mistake. monitors.conf describes
# physical displays per box, so it stays per-machine. input.conf used to be
# in this list too, but its current contents (kb_layout, kb_options, repeat
# rate, touchpad scroll factor, terminal scroll windowrules) are user
# preferences shared across machines, so it is now stow-managed.
monitors\.conf
